+## Reading — `the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p`, 2025-11-03, the Sensory Rulebook — a disembodied operating system whose ideal state is KW1, and an externalised perpetrator introject in KW3
+
+The essay opens AEGIS as „a disembodied operating system whose existence is predicated on enforcing coherence through the negation of entropy and contradiction“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L13], and calls the four worlds manifestations of Kael's inner landscape „under AEGIS's flawed control“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L13].
+
+KW1 is its ideal: „This world is AEGIS's ideal state, an attempt to enforce a rigid classical logic where the Law of Non-Contradiction is absolute and any deviation is an error to be corrected.“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L17] KW1's Guardian is „an agent embodying the strict, formal logic and unyielding order enforced by AEGIS.“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L19]
+
+In KW3 it is a psychological figure, not only a system: the protector alters' fortress shields the child parts from „the invalidating control of AEGIS, which functions as an“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L57] „externalisiertes Täterintrojekt“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L57], glossed in the text as externalized perpetrator introject.
+
+In the conclusion the body is set against it: „While AEGIS seeks a disembodied coherence through the top-down imposition of classical logic and the elimination of contradiction“ ^[the-sensory-rulebook-the-body-as-a-measuring-device-in-the-p.md:L111].
